/**
 * Support page — a company page under the portfolio hub, not a Card Games one,
 * so it wears hub chrome like About and the legal documents.
 *
 * Deliberately an address rather than a contact form. A form is a chain that
 * can break silently and lose a customer's message; mail cannot, and the
 * sender keeps their own copy. The "what to include" list recovers most of
 * what a form's required fields would have bought.
 *
 * This is also the Support URL that App Store Connect and Google Play both
 * ask for, which is why it answers the common questions rather than only
 * printing an address — most people arriving here want an answer, not a reply.
 *
 * The answers carry an FAQPage schema, so `npm run faq-audit` checks every
 * locale against English for drifted figures and mismatched questions. Keep
 * the groups the same length in every language, and write counts as numerals
 * everywhere ("3 games", not "three") so the audit can compare them.
 */
